 "_doc": "Casing rule (design/beta/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md §v2.6): UI labels are sentence case. At display time, sentenceCase() keeps the first letter of the label, any phrase below, any word below, and any word that is all-caps (BBQ, TV, UNESCO, UW) or a single capital letter (U-pick) or has an internal capital (MiMo, MetroParks, YouTube). Everything else after the first word is lowercased. Data files are never edited. Add a proper noun here (not in code) when a label needs it; design/beta/casing/sentence_case.py --check lists every change for review. A page's own place names keep their capitals as whole names, as runs of capitalised words, or as single words not in `generic`.",
